## 1. Verdict summary

The proposal is substantially source-correct. Every consequential source claim I re-fetched held at the stated pin, the issue/PR chains are real and correctly described, and the honest labels (source fact vs inference vs choice vs executed vs unexecuted) are used accurately throughout. I found **no fabricated source, no invented receipt, and no overreach of an executed witness**. I found two corrections (one pin mislabel in `sources.json`, one scope overstatement in what the v1.5.6 regression file can evidence), one stated uncertainty that is now **resolved by stronger evidence** (first release containing the C1 fix = v0.2.2), and three new evidence items that strengthen the proposal's own leads. Nothing found undermines the architecture or the data contract.

