## 3. Corrections (evidence-backed)

- **C-1 — `sources.json` S8 pin mislabeled the merge commit (must fix).** S8's pin reads "PR 1015 (merge commit 921d87713fd5052f5feed541cfdb2723b05a7a9e per blob URLs)". The PR API shows `merge_commit_sha` = `625b56f021ea19bc3181a60756801d746b2d1968`; `921d877…` is the PR **head** sha (it appears as `head.sha`/`statuses_url`, and as the second parent of merge commit 625b56f, whose message is "Merge pull request #1015 from cwida/ncvoter"). The blob URLs in `/files` reference the head sha, which is how the mislabel arose. Fix: S8 pin → "PR head 921d877…, merged as 625b56f… (2020-10-16)". Proposal prose never cites the sha, so no prose change; scope of impact is the catalog pin only. (Correcting the pin is not, by itself, evidence about anything else.)
- **C-2 — S9 scope overstatement (must fix).** At v1.5.6 the `test_sample_size.test` file exercises only **explicit** `SAMPLE_SIZE=1` and `SAMPLE_SIZE=-1`; its later blocks' comments still say "sample size 500 / 50 / 200 / 20" while every statement actually uses `SAMPLE_SIZE = -1`. So the file evidences (a) presence at the pin and (b) version-shifted expectations, but **not** default-`sample_size` behavior at v1.5.6. The proposal's §4 sentence stays true with this scope note added; it also *strengthens* P5, because the pin's own regression file no longer covers the default-sampling path that #25824 exercises.
- **C-3 — §14's stated uncertainty "first release containing the C1 fix is not established" is now resolved (apply the upgrade).** Compare-API ancestry: for `v0.2.1...625b56f` the merge-base is `d9bcedd` (v0.2.1 tip, 2020-08-29), `ahead_by 454` ⇒ the fix is **not** in v0.2.1; for `v0.2.2...625b56f` the merge-base is `625b56f` itself, `behind_by 288` ⇒ the fix **is** in v0.2.2 (tip `3222acc`, 2020-11-01); for `v0.2.3...625b56f`, merge-base again `625b56f`, `behind_by 818` ⇒ also in v0.2.3. First checked release containing the fix: **v0.2.2**. Residual limit (state it): releases between v0.2.1 and v0.2.2 were not exhaustively enumerated; the conclusion assumes the 0.2.1→0.2.2 tag sequence is consecutive.
- **C-4 — labeling precision (should fix).** §10's "so 3.15 is newest stable" is an inference from "main = 3.16" (V-9); that 3.15 has shipped is not in any captured bytes (the release-cycle table was beyond the delivered portion). Mark it [INF] and extend L2 to cover "3.15 released status + per-version EOL dates" together.

